---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';

const page = {
  title: "Write a Raspberry Pi image to an SD card — Bootable",
  description: "Download or open a Raspberry Pi image, write it to an SD card, and verify the written bytes.",
  ogTitle: "Write a Raspberry Pi image to an SD card",
  ogDescription: "Choose a Raspberry Pi image, write it to SD, and verify it.",
  ogType: "article",
  current: "guide",
  doc: { label: "Safety", href: "https://github.com/debpalash/bootable/blob/main/docs/safety.md" },
  crumbs: [{ label: "Home", href: "/" }, { label: "Guides", href: "/guides.html" }, { label: "Raspberry Pi image" }],
};
---
<Layout {...page}>
<main class="guide-main">
  <Breadcrumbs crumbs={page.crumbs} />
      <article>
        <header class="guide-hero"><p class="eyebrow">Raspberry Pi · IMG · SD</p><h1>Write a Raspberry Pi image to SD</h1><p class="lede">Choose an image, write it to an SD card, and verify the written bytes.</p></header>
        <div class="guide-body">
          <div class="guide-content">
            <h2 id="source">Choose a Raspberry Pi image</h2>
            <p>Use the Raspberry Pi catalog or open a local <code>.img</code>, <code>.raw</code>, or compressed file. Downloads can be paused, resumed, cancelled, or retried.</p>
            <p>Bootable verifies a publisher checksum when available. Otherwise, it labels the download HTTPS-only.</p>

            <h2 id="capacity">Check capacity</h2>
            <p>Bootable measures the expanded image and checks that it fits the card.</p>
            <p>Bad-block and fake-capacity tests erase the card. Use expendable media.</p>

            <h2 id="steps">Write the card</h2>
            <ol>
              <li>Choose a catalog image or local file.</li>
              <li>Insert the SD card through a removable or USB-attached reader.</li>
              <li>Select the whole card, not a mounted partition.</li>
              <li>Review the expanded size, physical target, and permanent erasure.</li>
              <li>Write and wait for read-back verification.</li>
            </ol>
            <div class="guide-callout"><p><strong>The whole card will be erased.</strong> Check the card and reader before writing.</p></div>

            <h2 id="verification">Verify the write</h2>
            <p>Bootable reads back the written range and compares SHA-256. This does not confirm that the image supports your Pi model.</p>

            <h2 id="after">After the write</h2>
            <p>Wait for the safe-removal result. Rewrite the full image after a cancellation or verification failure.</p>

            <section class="related-guides"><h2>Related guides</h2><ul><li><a href="/compressed-image-writer">Write compressed images</a></li><li><a href="/verify-bootable-usb">Verification details</a></li><li><a href="/write-iso-to-usb">Write an ISO to USB</a></li></ul></section>
            <div class="guide-cta"><h2>Install Bootable</h2><p>Use the desktop app or TUI.</p><a class="button primary" href="/download">View install steps</a></div>
          </div>
          <aside class="guide-aside"><strong>On this page</strong><ul><li><a href="#source">Choose an image</a></li><li><a href="#capacity">Check capacity</a></li><li><a href="#steps">Write the card</a></li><li><a href="#verification">Verify the write</a></li><li><a href="#after">Safe removal</a></li></ul></aside>
        </div>
      </article>
</main>
</Layout>
